.TH KEYBOARDLIGHTS 1 "" "KeyboardLights" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keyboardlights \- configure lighting and key assignments on legacy Cloud Nine C989 keyboards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyboardlights
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
KeyboardLights is a GTK application for the legacy Cloud Nine C989 keyboard
with firmware 1.38. Revised hardware with firmware 1.82 is incompatible.
Run as your normal desktop user. Reconnect the keyboard after installation
or upgrade to activate the device access rule.
.PP
Settings load automatically when the keyboard is detected. Refresh reloads
settings while keeping staged edits. Previewing changes and opening profiles
do not update the keyboard. Review and explicitly apply changes to update it.
.SH USING THE APP
Choose Solid color to paint keys and adjust brightness, or an animation to
adjust its speed. The pointer selects a key without painting. The brush paints
individual keys; the bucket fills connected keys of the same color.
Clear starts a blank preview; Fill colors blank keys. Paint or fill every blank
key before saving a lighting profile or reviewing changes.
.PP
Select a key to edit its assignment below the keyboard. Choose Review changes,
check the summary, select the confirmation checkbox, then choose Apply changes.
If an update fails, the app stops and reports what completed.
.PP
Use File > Lighting Profile or File > Assignment Profile to create, open, save,
or delete profile files. Opening a profile stages its settings for review.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture " FILE"
Open a channel-1 lighting image for offline inspection. Device writes are disabled.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " DIRECTORY"
Choose the directory for preferences and optional diagnostic logs.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostic-logging
Save diagnostic logs for subsequent operations. Logging is disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-no-auto-read
Wait for Refresh instead of reading the keyboard on launch.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/KeyboardLights/Profiles
Default location for profile file dialogs. Uses
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
instead of ~/.config when set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/KeyboardLights
Preferences and optional diagnostic records. Uses
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
instead of ~/.local/state when set.
.PP
Removing or purging the package preserves user profiles, preferences, and logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/keyboardlights/README
.PP
Help > About shows the installed app version and license.
